VALUES ('9d26dbfb-62fd-4035-a6c3-c4bbc4dbf488', 'terraform-validation-lifecycle-ephemeral', 'Terraform Associate Practice: Validation, Lifecycle & Ephemeral Values', 'terraform', ARRAY['Terraform Associate', 'Validation', 'Lifecycle', 'Ephemeral Values']::TEXT[], 38, 'advanced', true, 5, 60, 1, 0);

-- ── Section: Custom Validation Rules (11 questions) — Custom Validation Rules — authored from developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/language/values/variables, .../language/block/variable, and hashicorp.com/blog/terraform-1-9-enhances-input-variable-validations; verified via web search against current Terraform 1.9+/1.12 docs, not copied from any official HashiCorp exam material. ──

VALUES ('efc78d74-f3e7-40e2-94dc-d719f5a9921b', '9d26dbfb-62fd-4035-a6c3-c4bbc4dbf488', 1, 'What are the two required arguments inside a variable''s ''validation'' block?', 'Validation', 'Validation Block Required Arguments', 'mcq');
VALUES ('efc78d74-f3e7-40e2-94dc-d719f5a9921b', 'dc10fc16-9697-433d-8f23-00cccd201274', 'A validation block requires exactly two arguments: condition (a boolean expression) and error_message (the string shown when condition evaluates to false).', 'Custom Validation Rules — authored from developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/language/values/variables, .../language/block/variable, and hashicorp.com/blog/terraform-1-9-enhances-input-variable-validations; verified via web search against current Terraform 1.9+/1.12 docs, not copied from any official HashiCorp exam material.');

VALUES ('6097cd6b-0c72-4659-a1a0-786eae9000ff', '9d26dbfb-62fd-4035-a6c3-c4bbc4dbf488', 2, 'Can a single input variable declare more than one ''validation'' block?', 'Validation', 'Multiple Validation Blocks', 'mcq');
VALUES ('6097cd6b-0c72-4659-a1a0-786eae9000ff', '26797be2-ba00-411f-9343-67987c1d12b2', 'Terraform allows multiple validation blocks on the same variable; each is evaluated independently and reports its own error_message if its condition fails, which is often clearer than one large compound condition.', 'Custom Validation Rules — authored from developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/language/values/variables, .../language/block/variable, and hashicorp.com/blog/terraform-1-9-enhances-input-variable-validations; verified via web search against current Terraform 1.9+/1.12 docs, not copied from any official HashiCorp exam material.');

VALUES ('9ce1743d-14ad-4071-8951-cab51b8beab5', '9d26dbfb-62fd-4035-a6c3-c4bbc4dbf488', 3, 'At what point does Terraform evaluate a variable''s validation block(s)?', 'Validation', 'Validation Timing', 'mcq');
VALUES ('9ce1743d-14ad-4071-8951-cab51b8beab5', 'eba9ef47-8cc7-4a6f-9bed-81f70ab47c70', 'Variable validations run early during plan (once the variable''s value is known), before Terraform evaluates the rest of the configuration that depends on it.', 'Custom Validation Rules — authored from developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/language/values/variables, .../language/block/variable, and hashicorp.com/blog/terraform-1-9-enhances-input-variable-validations; verified via web search against current Terraform 1.9+/1.12 docs, not copied from any official HashiCorp exam material.');

VALUES ('2f27ddba-bac9-40fb-90ee-06a5fe3c27f2', '9d26dbfb-62fd-4035-a6c3-c4bbc4dbf488', 4, 'As of Terraform 1.9, what changed about what a variable''s validation condition is allowed to reference?', 'Validation', 'Cross-Variable Validation (1.9+)', 'mcq');
VALUES ('2f27ddba-bac9-40fb-90ee-06a5fe3c27f2', '09fe8925-3274-4cd1-b506-c8ce9ee38d2f', 'Terraform 1.9 lifted the earlier restriction that a validation condition could only reference the variable itself, allowing conditions to also consider other variables, data sources, and locals — enabling genuine cross-variable validation.', 'Custom Validation Rules — authored from developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/language/values/variables, .../language/block/variable, and hashicorp.com/blog/terraform-1-9-enhances-input-variable-validations; verified via web search against current Terraform 1.9+/1.12 docs, not copied from any official HashiCorp exam material.');

VALUES ('82fc2a25-fd79-421f-b598-82936ea0886c', '9d26dbfb-62fd-4035-a6c3-c4bbc4dbf488', 5, 'A variable''s validation block now (Terraform 1.9+) references only var.enable_feature and var.other_setting, but never references the variable it''s actually attached to. What happens?', 'Validation', 'Cross-Variable Validation Constraint', 'mcq');
VALUES ('82fc2a25-fd79-421f-b598-82936ea0886c', 'b2ae6199-2991-4b86-9f0b-895b9940c242', 'Being able to reference other variables/data sources/locals doesn''t remove the requirement that the condition also reference the variable it''s declared on — a validation block that never mentions its own variable is rejected.', 'Custom Validation Rules — authored from developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/language/values/variables, .../language/block/variable, and hashicorp.com/blog/terraform-1-9-enhances-input-variable-validations; verified via web search against current Terraform 1.9+/1.12 docs, not copied from any official HashiCorp exam material.');

VALUES ('835a66bd-9a01-48d2-a770-fc810cc0155d', '9d26dbfb-62fd-4035-a6c3-c4bbc4dbf488', 6, 'A variable is declared with type = number. Why might you still add a validation block on top of that type constraint, e.g. requiring the number be between 1 and 100?', 'Validation', 'Validation vs. Type Constraints', 'mcq');
VALUES ('835a66bd-9a01-48d2-a770-fc810cc0155d', '53940039-7960-4e27-bb9b-3fcfe40dce6d', 'Type constraints only enforce the value''s shape/type; a validation block is needed to enforce domain-specific rules like numeric ranges, allowed strings, or cross-field consistency.', 'Custom Validation Rules — authored from developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/language/values/variables, .../language/block/variable, and hashicorp.com/blog/terraform-1-9-enhances-input-variable-validations; verified via web search against current Terraform 1.9+/1.12 docs, not copied from any official HashiCorp exam material.');

VALUES ('d7344836-8532-4275-8ba3-d738f0a0bc0d', '9d26dbfb-62fd-4035-a6c3-c4bbc4dbf488', 7, 'You need a variable''s validation to fail unless BOTH of two independent conditions hold. Besides writing two separate validation blocks, what''s a common way to express this in a single condition?', 'Validation', 'Multi-Condition Validation', 'mcq');
VALUES ('d7344836-8532-4275-8ba3-d738f0a0bc0d', 'eec1fede-4f12-4fe0-a6af-8dfe6006e0b9', 'A single condition can combine multiple boolean checks with && (logical AND) or alltrue([...]) so the whole validation block fails unless every sub-condition is satisfied.', 'Custom Validation Rules — authored from developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/language/values/variables, .../language/block/variable, and hashicorp.com/blog/terraform-1-9-enhances-input-variable-validations; verified via web search against current Terraform 1.9+/1.12 docs, not copied from any official HashiCorp exam material.');

VALUES ('f9056f48-1f4c-46d9-bdb0-5e22f25d6ed6', '9d26dbfb-62fd-4035-a6c3-c4bbc4dbf488', 8, 'Can a validation block''s condition inspect elements inside a variable declared with a complex type, e.g. list(object({ name = string, port = number }))?', 'Validation', 'Validation on Complex Types', 'mcq');
VALUES ('f9056f48-1f4c-46d9-bdb0-5e22f25d6ed6', 'e3906540-820b-47ac-8c48-c7596e879392', 'Validation conditions are ordinary Terraform expressions, so they can use for-expressions and functions like alltrue() to check every element of a complex-typed variable, not just primitives.', 'Custom Validation Rules — authored from developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/language/values/variables, .../language/block/variable, and hashicorp.com/blog/terraform-1-9-enhances-input-variable-validations; verified via web search against current Terraform 1.9+/1.12 docs, not copied from any official HashiCorp exam material.');

VALUES ('eb6b10a8-4e80-43a1-8b3e-503d42f16ec6', '9d26dbfb-62fd-4035-a6c3-c4bbc4dbf488', 9, 'What is the error_message argument in a validation block used for?', 'Validation', 'error_message Content', 'mcq');
VALUES ('eb6b10a8-4e80-43a1-8b3e-503d42f16ec6', 'f1a7b2c3-f5f8-4102-8c0a-767a70b3afc6', 'error_message is purely a user-facing string explaining why the value failed validation — it plays no role in the pass/fail logic itself, which is entirely determined by condition.', 'Custom Validation Rules — authored from developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/language/values/variables, .../language/block/variable, and hashicorp.com/blog/terraform-1-9-enhances-input-variable-validations; verified via web search against current Terraform 1.9+/1.12 docs, not copied from any official HashiCorp exam material.');

VALUES ('c7a90234-cd44-4745-b3a6-98f557649ae7', '9d26dbfb-62fd-4035-a6c3-c4bbc4dbf488', 10, 'When a variable''s validation condition evaluates to false, what happens to the Terraform run?', 'Validation', 'Validation Failure Behavior', 'mcq');
VALUES ('c7a90234-cd44-4745-b3a6-98f557649ae7', '63335c84-dc48-48a3-91fe-0b8bef15fbaf', 'A failed validation is a hard stop — Terraform reports the error_message and aborts the plan; it does not continue with an invalid value or fall back silently.', 'Custom Validation Rules — authored from developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/language/values/variables, .../language/block/variable, and hashicorp.com/blog/terraform-1-9-enhances-input-variable-validations; verified via web search against current Terraform 1.9+/1.12 docs, not copied from any official HashiCorp exam material.');

VALUES ('c579ad03-da71-4c04-a6e4-a5cef94b685c', '9d26dbfb-62fd-4035-a6c3-c4bbc4dbf488', 11, 'Can a variable be marked both ''sensitive = true'' (or ''ephemeral = true'') AND still have a validation block?', 'Validation', 'Validation vs. sensitive/ephemeral', 'mcq');
VALUES ('c579ad03-da71-4c04-a6e4-a5cef94b685c', 'b3b968fe-a6b2-4cc2-87e0-0752f6592b27', 'sensitive and ephemeral control how a value is displayed/persisted, which is orthogonal to validation, which checks the value''s content — both can be applied to the same variable.', 'Custom Validation Rules — authored from developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/language/values/variables, .../language/block/variable, and hashicorp.com/blog/terraform-1-9-enhances-input-variable-validations; verified via web search against current Terraform 1.9+/1.12 docs, not copied from any official HashiCorp exam material.');

-- ── Section: Lifecycle Meta-Arguments & Custom Conditions (13 questions) — Lifecycle Meta-Arguments & Custom Conditions — authored from developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/language/meta-arguments/lifecycle and .../language/expressions/custom-conditions; verified via web search against current Terraform docs, not copied from any official HashiCorp exam material. ──

VALUES ('719a2bcd-0d76-4eb1-9339-d33693defc35', '9d26dbfb-62fd-4035-a6c3-c4bbc4dbf488', 12, 'A resource change requires replacement, and the resource has ''lifecycle { create_before_destroy = true }''. What order does Terraform use?', 'Lifecycle', 'create_before_destroy', 'mcq');
VALUES ('719a2bcd-0d76-4eb1-9339-d33693defc35', 'dea0f16e-f747-40fb-b30d-15d37d1b6bb5', 'create_before_destroy reverses Terraform''s default destroy-then-create replacement order, creating the new resource before removing the old one — useful for minimizing downtime.', 'Lifecycle Meta-Arguments & Custom Conditions — authored from developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/language/meta-arguments/lifecycle and .../language/expressions/custom-conditions; verified via web search against current Terraform docs, not copied from any official HashiCorp exam material.');

VALUES ('5321a585-bb48-4545-8fc9-ce81c084cdfb', '9d26dbfb-62fd-4035-a6c3-c4bbc4dbf488', 13, 'A resource has ''lifecycle { prevent_destroy = true }''. What happens if a plan would destroy that resource (e.g. its resource block is removed from configuration)?', 'Lifecycle', 'prevent_destroy', 'mcq');
VALUES ('5321a585-bb48-4545-8fc9-ce81c084cdfb', '9a36ecaa-5a90-4e21-a062-4d33990f1a9e', 'prevent_destroy acts as a safety guard: any plan that would destroy the resource (including one caused by removing it from configuration) is rejected with an error instead of proceeding.', 'Lifecycle Meta-Arguments & Custom Conditions — authored from developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/language/meta-arguments/lifecycle and .../language/expressions/custom-conditions; verified via web search against current Terraform docs, not copied from any official HashiCorp exam material.');

VALUES ('155bc05a-9f7e-4c81-9ff1-1b428e0a1595', '9d26dbfb-62fd-4035-a6c3-c4bbc4dbf488', 14, 'A resource has ''lifecycle { ignore_changes = [tags] }''. What effect does this have?', 'Lifecycle', 'ignore_changes', 'mcq');
VALUES ('155bc05a-9f7e-4c81-9ff1-1b428e0a1595', 'a5b74209-b753-4774-8e23-62ad050ae706', 'ignore_changes tells Terraform to exclude the listed attribute(s) from diff calculations after creation, so changes made outside Terraform (or intentionally left alone) don''t keep showing up as drift.', 'Lifecycle Meta-Arguments & Custom Conditions — authored from developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/language/meta-arguments/lifecycle and .../language/expressions/custom-conditions; verified via web search against current Terraform docs, not copied from any official HashiCorp exam material.');

VALUES ('16f46df0-c057-45b4-9627-7e5b38111180', '9d26dbfb-62fd-4035-a6c3-c4bbc4dbf488', 15, 'What does setting ''lifecycle { ignore_changes = all }'' do, as opposed to listing specific attribute names?', 'Lifecycle', 'ignore_changes = all', 'mcq');
VALUES ('16f46df0-c057-45b4-9627-7e5b38111180', '16dd0fe8-e71d-443a-b8db-78a28f56036e', 'The special value ''all'' in ignore_changes applies the ignore behavior to every attribute on the resource, not just a specific list — useful when an external process manages most of the resource''s fields.', 'Lifecycle Meta-Arguments & Custom Conditions — authored from developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/language/meta-arguments/lifecycle and .../language/expressions/custom-conditions; verified via web search against current Terraform docs, not copied from any official HashiCorp exam material.');

VALUES ('a96546e9-c2e7-4878-810d-d111a1bf52b5', '9d26dbfb-62fd-4035-a6c3-c4bbc4dbf488', 16, 'What does the ''replace_triggered_by'' lifecycle argument do?', 'Lifecycle', 'replace_triggered_by', 'mcq');
VALUES ('a96546e9-c2e7-4878-810d-d111a1bf52b5', 'e713af7e-5787-4669-8346-6447e479ae59', 'replace_triggered_by lets a resource be forced into replacement based on changes to something else entirely (e.g. a related resource or attribute), not just its own argument changes.', 'Lifecycle Meta-Arguments & Custom Conditions — authored from developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/language/meta-arguments/lifecycle and .../language/expressions/custom-conditions; verified via web search against current Terraform docs, not copied from any official HashiCorp exam material.');

VALUES ('8db3c418-0e7b-452c-a3a6-e7d14e3c306e', '9d26dbfb-62fd-4035-a6c3-c4bbc4dbf488', 17, 'What kinds of references can be listed in a resource''s ''replace_triggered_by'' argument?', 'Lifecycle', 'replace_triggered_by Reference Types', 'mcq');
VALUES ('8db3c418-0e7b-452c-a3a6-e7d14e3c306e', 'b09bbfbd-7421-4c69-a481-411fc0105296', 'replace_triggered_by accepts references to specific resource attributes or to whole resources — referencing a whole resource means ANY change to that resource (including it being recreated) triggers replacement.', 'Lifecycle Meta-Arguments & Custom Conditions — authored from developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/language/meta-arguments/lifecycle and .../language/expressions/custom-conditions; verified via web search against current Terraform docs, not copied from any official HashiCorp exam material.');

VALUES ('fc3995aa-08f0-4be3-91ee-4e3a787d2c50', '9d26dbfb-62fd-4035-a6c3-c4bbc4dbf488', 18, 'Which of these is NOT one of the standard lifecycle meta-arguments available on a resource block (as opposed to precondition/postcondition, which nest inside lifecycle but are their own construct)?', 'Lifecycle', 'Five Lifecycle Meta-Arguments', 'mcq');
VALUES ('fc3995aa-08f0-4be3-91ee-4e3a787d2c50', '97b2ba8f-2219-4dd0-acb7-9887df884a5e', 'depends_on is its own top-level meta-argument on the resource block, not nested inside lifecycle {}. The four core lifecycle settings are create_before_destroy, prevent_destroy, ignore_changes, and replace_triggered_by.', 'Lifecycle Meta-Arguments & Custom Conditions — authored from developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/language/meta-arguments/lifecycle and .../language/expressions/custom-conditions; verified via web search against current Terraform docs, not copied from any official HashiCorp exam material.');

VALUES ('09f5ebaa-e8e7-4de8-831b-be8716b7fc0e', '9d26dbfb-62fd-4035-a6c3-c4bbc4dbf488', 19, 'Where is the ''depends_on'' meta-argument declared relative to ''lifecycle { }''?', 'Lifecycle', 'depends_on Placement', 'mcq');
VALUES ('09f5ebaa-e8e7-4de8-831b-be8716b7fc0e', '371462a2-dc18-481f-8c43-aba7d8788ad3', 'depends_on sits directly in the resource/module block as its own meta-argument, distinct from the lifecycle {} block that holds create_before_destroy/prevent_destroy/ignore_changes/replace_triggered_by and the precondition/postcondition sub-blocks.', 'Lifecycle Meta-Arguments & Custom Conditions — authored from developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/language/meta-arguments/lifecycle and .../language/expressions/custom-conditions; verified via web search against current Terraform docs, not copied from any official HashiCorp exam material.');

VALUES ('ab89f6db-7f01-47a0-ae31-d83a96c99c1b', '9d26dbfb-62fd-4035-a6c3-c4bbc4dbf488', 20, 'Where are ''precondition'' and ''postcondition'' blocks declared in a resource, data source, or output?', 'Lifecycle', 'precondition/postcondition Location', 'mcq');
VALUES ('ab89f6db-7f01-47a0-ae31-d83a96c99c1b', 'a1985656-be11-4bcd-a853-e6f1d843ba35', 'Custom conditions are sub-blocks of lifecycle { } — e.g. resource "aws_instance" "x" { lifecycle { precondition { condition = ..., error_message = ... } } } — not standalone top-level blocks.', 'Lifecycle Meta-Arguments & Custom Conditions — authored from developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/language/meta-arguments/lifecycle and .../language/expressions/custom-conditions; verified via web search against current Terraform docs, not copied from any official HashiCorp exam material.');

VALUES ('6c9a6ee5-0481-442e-af8f-bcf0017db826', '9d26dbfb-62fd-4035-a6c3-c4bbc4dbf488', 21, 'When does a resource''s ''precondition'' block get evaluated, relative to that resource actually being created or updated?', 'Lifecycle', 'precondition Timing', 'mcq');
VALUES ('6c9a6ee5-0481-442e-af8f-bcf0017db826', 'c2ae5945-e60a-497b-9f5e-f0a6c203b75d', 'A precondition checks assumptions that must hold before Terraform proceeds to create or modify the resource — it runs post-plan but pre-apply for that resource.', 'Lifecycle Meta-Arguments & Custom Conditions — authored from developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/language/meta-arguments/lifecycle and .../language/expressions/custom-conditions; verified via web search against current Terraform docs, not copied from any official HashiCorp exam material.');

VALUES ('fa210457-8f94-4691-833b-83e8f4f5785b', '9d26dbfb-62fd-4035-a6c3-c4bbc4dbf488', 22, 'When does a resource''s ''postcondition'' block get evaluated?', 'Lifecycle', 'postcondition Timing', 'mcq');
VALUES ('fa210457-8f94-4691-833b-83e8f4f5785b', '25cb12d2-16ff-43ad-85f9-e07e1b04aaf1', 'Postconditions verify guarantees about the outcome — they run after the resource has actually been created/updated (or, for a data source, after it has been read).', 'Lifecycle Meta-Arguments & Custom Conditions — authored from developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/language/meta-arguments/lifecycle and .../language/expressions/custom-conditions; verified via web search against current Terraform docs, not copied from any official HashiCorp exam material.');

VALUES ('83a29412-7261-4316-b930-64b3f64d3c5b', '9d26dbfb-62fd-4035-a6c3-c4bbc4dbf488', 23, 'Why might you use a resource-level ''precondition'' instead of (or in addition to) an input variable''s ''validation'' block?', 'Lifecycle', 'precondition vs. Variable Validation', 'mcq');
VALUES ('83a29412-7261-4316-b930-64b3f64d3c5b', 'e5eeecae-a7c3-4170-a17a-d096f781e620', 'Variable validation only has access to the variable''s own value (plus, since 1.9, other referenceable objects known early); a resource''s precondition can check conditions involving that specific resource''s context, such as a related data source''s attributes, at the point just before that resource is acted on.', 'Lifecycle Meta-Arguments & Custom Conditions — authored from developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/language/meta-arguments/lifecycle and .../language/expressions/custom-conditions; verified via web search against current Terraform docs, not copied from any official HashiCorp exam material.');

VALUES ('2708291b-e415-4749-8770-c658f538f16c', '9d26dbfb-62fd-4035-a6c3-c4bbc4dbf488', 24, 'A postcondition on an aws_instance resource checks ''condition = self.private_ip != ""''. What does ''self'' refer to here?', 'Lifecycle', 'postcondition self_check Example', 'mcq');
VALUES ('2708291b-e415-4749-8770-c658f538f16c', '57cf055f-e0a3-410a-9b96-5fc89def817b', 'Inside a resource''s own postcondition, ''self'' refers to that resource itself, allowing the condition to check attributes of the resource that was just created/updated.', 'Lifecycle Meta-Arguments & Custom Conditions — authored from developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/language/meta-arguments/lifecycle and .../language/expressions/custom-conditions; verified via web search against current Terraform docs, not copied from any official HashiCorp exam material.');

-- ── Section: Ephemeral Values & Write-Only Arguments (14 questions) — Ephemeral Values & Write-Only Arguments — authored from developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/language/manage-sensitive-data/ephemeral, .../language/block/ephemeral, .../language/functions/ephemeralasnull, and .../plugin/framework/resources/write-only-arguments; verified via web search against current Terraform 1.10-1.12 docs (this feature postdates most pretrained knowledge), not copied from any official HashiCorp exam material. ──

VALUES ('0e31f156-b4b4-4451-84db-650711855671', '9d26dbfb-62fd-4035-a6c3-c4bbc4dbf488', 25, 'What is an ''ephemeral value'' in Terraform, at its core?', 'Ephemeral Values', 'Ephemeral Values Definition', 'mcq');
VALUES ('0e31f156-b4b4-4451-84db-650711855671', '54f70947-62eb-42d7-ae98-1d0bca874147', 'Ephemeral values are Terraform''s mechanism for handling data (like short-lived credentials) that should never be written to state or plan files, existing only for the duration of the operation that needs them.', 'Ephemeral Values & Write-Only Arguments — authored from developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/language/manage-sensitive-data/ephemeral, .../language/block/ephemeral, .../language/functions/ephemeralasnull, and .../plugin/framework/resources/write-only-arguments; verified via web search against current Terraform 1.10-1.12 docs (this feature postdates most pretrained knowledge), not copied from any official HashiCorp exam material.');

VALUES ('351220c4-216b-4220-857f-966025982b0d', '9d26dbfb-62fd-4035-a6c3-c4bbc4dbf488', 26, 'What is the correct syntax for declaring an ephemeral resource?', 'Ephemeral Values', 'Ephemeral Resource Block Syntax', 'mcq');
VALUES ('351220c4-216b-4220-857f-966025982b0d', '4d79d9eb-8082-4496-a86a-c29b35f43439', 'Ephemeral resources use their own top-level block type, ''ephemeral'', with the same two-label syntax pattern as resource and data blocks: ephemeral "<TYPE>" "<LABEL>" { }.', 'Ephemeral Values & Write-Only Arguments — authored from developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/language/manage-sensitive-data/ephemeral, .../language/block/ephemeral, .../language/functions/ephemeralasnull, and .../plugin/framework/resources/write-only-arguments; verified via web search against current Terraform 1.10-1.12 docs (this feature postdates most pretrained knowledge), not copied from any official HashiCorp exam material.');

VALUES ('6b0f3bea-8c63-4577-b18c-597ad931d3e0', '9d26dbfb-62fd-4035-a6c3-c4bbc4dbf488', 27, 'Where do the available ephemeral resource TYPEs (e.g. an ephemeral ''random_password'' or an ephemeral secret-fetching resource) come from?', 'Ephemeral Values', 'Who Defines Ephemeral Resource Types', 'mcq');
VALUES ('6b0f3bea-8c63-4577-b18c-597ad931d3e0', '2c86d7db-95f4-4e3d-8a9f-27d54dae56cf', 'Like managed resources and data sources, ephemeral resource types are defined by provider developers — a provider must explicitly implement an ephemeral resource type for it to be usable.', 'Ephemeral Values & Write-Only Arguments — authored from developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/language/manage-sensitive-data/ephemeral, .../language/block/ephemeral, .../language/functions/ephemeralasnull, and .../plugin/framework/resources/write-only-arguments; verified via web search against current Terraform 1.10-1.12 docs (this feature postdates most pretrained knowledge), not copied from any official HashiCorp exam material.');

VALUES ('3454cd78-7854-4366-9041-1a43f57a90c3', '9d26dbfb-62fd-4035-a6c3-c4bbc4dbf488', 28, 'How do you reference an attribute of a declared ephemeral resource, e.g. one named ''db_password'' of type ''random_password''?', 'Ephemeral Values', 'Referencing an Ephemeral Resource', 'mcq');
VALUES ('3454cd78-7854-4366-9041-1a43f57a90c3', 'e921e2bf-6f68-4490-a12a-c317d801adc2', 'Ephemeral resources are referenced with the pattern ephemeral.<TYPE>.<LABEL>.<ATTRIBUTE> — analogous to how a data source is referenced as data.<TYPE>.<LABEL>.<ATTRIBUTE>.', 'Ephemeral Values & Write-Only Arguments — authored from developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/language/manage-sensitive-data/ephemeral, .../language/block/ephemeral, .../language/functions/ephemeralasnull, and .../plugin/framework/resources/write-only-arguments; verified via web search against current Terraform 1.10-1.12 docs (this feature postdates most pretrained knowledge), not copied from any official HashiCorp exam material.');

VALUES ('289a31f6-3342-46cc-b8dc-8530abc148e9', '9d26dbfb-62fd-4035-a6c3-c4bbc4dbf488', 29, 'Are ephemeral resources ever recorded in Terraform''s state file?', 'Ephemeral Values', 'Ephemeral Resource State Storage', 'mcq');
VALUES ('289a31f6-3342-46cc-b8dc-8530abc148e9', 'aacd3347-8aed-46cb-9b43-f08119042c40', 'Ephemeral resources are fundamentally defined by NOT being persisted — Terraform doesn''t record them in state or plan files at all, which is the entire point of the feature.', 'Ephemeral Values & Write-Only Arguments — authored from developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/language/manage-sensitive-data/ephemeral, .../language/block/ephemeral, .../language/functions/ephemeralasnull, and .../plugin/framework/resources/write-only-arguments; verified via web search against current Terraform 1.10-1.12 docs (this feature postdates most pretrained knowledge), not copied from any official HashiCorp exam material.');

VALUES ('07e9b83a-3749-4186-bec3-88af0505df44', '9d26dbfb-62fd-4035-a6c3-c4bbc4dbf488', 30, 'What is the documented lifecycle of an ephemeral resource across a Terraform operation?', 'Ephemeral Values', 'Ephemeral Resource Lifecycle', 'mcq');
VALUES ('07e9b83a-3749-4186-bec3-88af0505df44', 'd3c4886e-2418-458a-b206-53885fdccf13', 'Ephemeral resources follow their own open/renew/close lifecycle: Terraform opens them when their result is needed, may ask the provider to periodically renew access, and closes them once the current run phase''s dependent work is done.', 'Ephemeral Values & Write-Only Arguments — authored from developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/language/manage-sensitive-data/ephemeral, .../language/block/ephemeral, .../language/functions/ephemeralasnull, and .../plugin/framework/resources/write-only-arguments; verified via web search against current Terraform 1.10-1.12 docs (this feature postdates most pretrained knowledge), not copied from any official HashiCorp exam material.');

VALUES ('85f18ce9-7f2b-4fbb-b8d2-ea2382289971', '9d26dbfb-62fd-4035-a6c3-c4bbc4dbf488', 31, 'In which Terraform version were write-only arguments on managed resources introduced?', 'Ephemeral Values', 'Write-Only Arguments Introduction', 'mcq');
VALUES ('85f18ce9-7f2b-4fbb-b8d2-ea2382289971', '295e003e-7a8c-4c8f-bf8d-cfe917e59b8d', 'Write-only arguments (accepting ephemeral or non-ephemeral values on ordinary managed resources) were introduced in Terraform 1.11, building on 1.10''s ephemeral values foundation.', 'Ephemeral Values & Write-Only Arguments — authored from developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/language/manage-sensitive-data/ephemeral, .../language/block/ephemeral, .../language/functions/ephemeralasnull, and .../plugin/framework/resources/write-only-arguments; verified via web search against current Terraform 1.10-1.12 docs (this feature postdates most pretrained knowledge), not copied from any official HashiCorp exam material.');

VALUES ('1fa5099f-e4a2-4549-9192-7ef0677f13e2', '9d26dbfb-62fd-4035-a6c3-c4bbc4dbf488', 32, 'What value does Terraform record in state for a write-only argument (e.g. a provider-defined ''password_wo'' attribute)?', 'Ephemeral Values', 'Write-Only Argument State Behavior', 'mcq');
VALUES ('1fa5099f-e4a2-4549-9192-7ef0677f13e2', '07104470-4789-41ce-9c63-8dfb89ca61e5', 'Write-only arguments are defined so that their prior, planned, and final state values are always null — the actual value is sent to the provider for the operation and never persisted.', 'Ephemeral Values & Write-Only Arguments — authored from developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/language/manage-sensitive-data/ephemeral, .../language/block/ephemeral, .../language/functions/ephemeralasnull, and .../plugin/framework/resources/write-only-arguments; verified via web search against current Terraform 1.10-1.12 docs (this feature postdates most pretrained knowledge), not copied from any official HashiCorp exam material.');

VALUES ('4b0be3de-3464-4e46-8139-cf21278b16ed', '9d26dbfb-62fd-4035-a6c3-c4bbc4dbf488', 33, 'Since a write-only argument''s state value is always null, why is it conventionally paired with a companion argument like ''password_wo_version''?', 'Ephemeral Values', 'Why Write-Only Args Need a Companion Trigger', 'mcq');
VALUES ('4b0be3de-3464-4e46-8139-cf21278b16ed', '86166a19-a735-47bb-89e0-1bcab6f8edcb', 'Because write-only values never show up as a state diff on their own (always null-to-null), providers rely on a companion argument the practitioner changes deliberately (like a version counter) to know when to re-send/re-apply the write-only value.', 'Ephemeral Values & Write-Only Arguments — authored from developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/language/manage-sensitive-data/ephemeral, .../language/block/ephemeral, .../language/functions/ephemeralasnull, and .../plugin/framework/resources/write-only-arguments; verified via web search against current Terraform 1.10-1.12 docs (this feature postdates most pretrained knowledge), not copied from any official HashiCorp exam material.');

VALUES ('66731f9a-6c1e-4c1d-b0c5-b7e3b6f9ce42', '9d26dbfb-62fd-4035-a6c3-c4bbc4dbf488', 34, 'Can a write-only argument accept a non-ephemeral (ordinary, persistent) value, or must its source always be an ephemeral value/resource?', 'Ephemeral Values', 'Write-Only Args and Ephemeral Values', 'mcq');
VALUES ('66731f9a-6c1e-4c1d-b0c5-b7e3b6f9ce42', '02cc82ab-0097-40b1-97f7-536d3ce06109', 'Write-only arguments are compatible with ephemeral values (which is their main use case for secrets) but aren''t restricted to them — they can also just take an ordinary non-ephemeral value if that''s what''s supplied.', 'Ephemeral Values & Write-Only Arguments — authored from developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/language/manage-sensitive-data/ephemeral, .../language/block/ephemeral, .../language/functions/ephemeralasnull, and .../plugin/framework/resources/write-only-arguments; verified via web search against current Terraform 1.10-1.12 docs (this feature postdates most pretrained knowledge), not copied from any official HashiCorp exam material.');

VALUES ('37677054-84d7-4d4b-b1fd-3c323d949778', '9d26dbfb-62fd-4035-a6c3-c4bbc4dbf488', 35, 'Which of the following is a documented restriction on write-only arguments?', 'Ephemeral Values', 'Write-Only Argument Restrictions', 'mcq');
VALUES ('37677054-84d7-4d4b-b1fd-3c323d949778', 'b880160d-24d5-4f5d-8e83-bc300743d3b7', 'Write-only arguments are explicitly documented as incompatible with set-based attribute/block types (set attributes, set nested attributes, set nested blocks), among other structural restrictions.', 'Ephemeral Values & Write-Only Arguments — authored from developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/language/manage-sensitive-data/ephemeral, .../language/block/ephemeral, .../language/functions/ephemeralasnull, and .../plugin/framework/resources/write-only-arguments; verified via web search against current Terraform 1.10-1.12 docs (this feature postdates most pretrained knowledge), not copied from any official HashiCorp exam material.');

VALUES ('6b76d353-8386-4529-b1c0-4407da6532fb', '9d26dbfb-62fd-4035-a6c3-c4bbc4dbf488', 36, 'What does the ''ephemeralasnull()'' function do?', 'Ephemeral Values', 'ephemeralasnull() Purpose', 'mcq');
VALUES ('6b76d353-8386-4529-b1c0-4407da6532fb', 'abc2e22a-0df3-4d94-9be6-b86fc6fc2659', 'ephemeralasnull() takes an ephemeral value and returns null, which is useful when you need to satisfy a context that can''t accept an ephemeral value but where null is an acceptable substitute — it nullifies rather than ''unwraps'' the ephemeral value.', 'Ephemeral Values & Write-Only Arguments — authored from developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/language/manage-sensitive-data/ephemeral, .../language/block/ephemeral, .../language/functions/ephemeralasnull, and .../plugin/framework/resources/write-only-arguments; verified via web search against current Terraform 1.10-1.12 docs (this feature postdates most pretrained knowledge), not copied from any official HashiCorp exam material.');

VALUES ('dc9300ba-d397-458b-a45b-ae75a5d7d687', '9d26dbfb-62fd-4035-a6c3-c4bbc4dbf488', 37, 'Since which Terraform version has the ''ephemeralasnull()'' function been available?', 'Ephemeral Values', 'ephemeralasnull() Version', 'mcq');
VALUES ('dc9300ba-d397-458b-a45b-ae75a5d7d687', '328331b6-34b5-4001-a5a0-d804d2d0f0ea', 'ephemeralasnull() shipped alongside the initial ephemeral values feature in Terraform 1.10, ahead of write-only arguments'' arrival in 1.11.', 'Ephemeral Values & Write-Only Arguments — authored from developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/language/manage-sensitive-data/ephemeral, .../language/block/ephemeral, .../language/functions/ephemeralasnull, and .../plugin/framework/resources/write-only-arguments; verified via web search against current Terraform 1.10-1.12 docs (this feature postdates most pretrained knowledge), not copied from any official HashiCorp exam material.');

VALUES ('c012d33d-9fa5-43cb-b290-b8449d78c269', '9d26dbfb-62fd-4035-a6c3-c4bbc4dbf488', 38, 'Can an ephemeral value be assigned directly to a root module''s regular output value?', 'Ephemeral Values', 'Ephemeral Values in Outputs', 'mcq');
VALUES ('c012d33d-9fa5-43cb-b290-b8449d78c269', '1eb7735a-f7a5-45ad-acf0-71f65c06504c', 'Ephemeral values can''t leak into persisted state via a normal output. An output must itself be marked ephemeral to legitimately hold one (or the value must be stripped down to null first).', 'Ephemeral Values & Write-Only Arguments — authored from developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/language/manage-sensitive-data/ephemeral, .../language/block/ephemeral, .../language/functions/ephemeralasnull, and .../plugin/framework/resources/write-only-arguments; verified via web search against current Terraform 1.10-1.12 docs (this feature postdates most pretrained knowledge), not copied from any official HashiCorp exam material.');
